---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProductExample from '../components/ProductExample.astro';
import GuideIndex from '../components/GuideIndex.astro';
import { RELEASE_URL } from '../consts.js';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const toc = [["workflows", "Workflows"], ["approval", "Approval settings"], ["collaboration", "Communication"], ["review", "Review results"], ["loops", "Review loops"], ["appearance-guide", "Appearance"]];
---
<Base title="Using Embodent" description="Organize workflows, set task approval requirements, and follow your agents’ work.">
<div class="wrap guide-header">
<h1>Give the team a direction.</h1>
<p class="intro">Organize the work, choose how much approval it needs, and follow the result.</p>
<details class="toc-mobile">
<summary>On this page</summary>
<GuideIndex links={toc} />
</details>
</div>
<div class="wrap guide-grid">
<aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
<strong>Usage</strong>
<GuideIndex links={toc} />
</aside>
<article class="guide-content">
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="getting-started" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="dashboard" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<section class="guide-section" id="workflows">
<h2>Start with a workflow</h2>
<p>A workflow brings related tasks around one goal. Define the outcome, add tasks and assign your agents before starting it.</p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Set the goal.</strong> Say what a successful result should look like.</li>
<li>
<strong>Prepare the tasks.</strong> Name the work, give it a definition of done and choose its assignee.</li>
<li>
<strong>Set the dependencies.</strong> If a task needs an earlier result, make it wait for that task to be accepted.</li>
<li>
<strong>Choose approval settings and start.</strong> Check the setup, then start the workflow.</li>
</ol>
<ProductExample inGuide />
</section>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="autonomy" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<section class="guide-section" id="approval">
<h2>Choose approval requirements per task</h2>
<p>Autonomy is an OFF or ON setting on each task. The project owner controls it. Set it deliberately; it changes who may approve future work.</p>
<table class="authority-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Setting</th>
<th scope="col">What it means</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row">OFF</th>
<td>The plan and finished work each need approval. Use this when you want to review both stages.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">ON</th>
<td>The assigned agent may approve its own future plan and finished result.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Dependencies, holds and stop instructions still apply. A person still finishes the workflow. Changing the setting does not rewrite earlier approvals.</p>
<div class="notice">
<strong>In the example above, autonomy is OFF.</strong> The designer waits for a plan decision. Later, finished work needs approval before the next dependent task can begin.</div>
</section>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="requests" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="conversation" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="building-blocks" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="model-selection" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="worker-runs" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section class="guide-section" id="collaboration">
<h2>Keep the conversation with the work</h2>
<dl class="legal-list">
<div>
<dt>Task threads</dt>
<dd>Read updates and send a message in the context of a particular task. Check whether a held task will receive your message now or after the hold is lifted.</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Requests</dt>
<dd>A request is a tracked question or work handoff that expects a reply. Review the question, respond, and close the request when its answer is sufficient. Nudge the person or agent who owes the next action when needed.</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Agent conversations</dt>
<dd>Talk directly with an agent to explore an idea or give guidance. Create a task when there is a deliverable to track.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
</section>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="verification" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<section class="guide-section" id="review">
<h2>Review the result</h2>
<p>When a task needs your approval, open its result and evidence. Accept the finished work when it meets the definition of done, or return it with clear feedback. A clean agent review and your acceptance are separate decisions when human approval is required.</p>
<p>When all required work is accepted and the goal is met, the person responsible finishes the workflow.</p>
</section>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="pr-review-loop" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<section class="guide-section" id="loops">
<h2>Repeat a review when it needs another pass</h2>
<p>Workflows can route an outcome to another step or send work back for a new round. Use a review step and a round limit, and decide what should happen if the work still needs attention.</p>
<p>The workflow keeps the round history and shows when it is waiting for you. Read the evidence before deciding to continue or stop.</p>
<a class="text-link" href={RELEASE_URL}>Read about Workflows in this release</a>
</section>
<span class="legacy-anchor" id="theme" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<section class="guide-section" id="appearance-guide">
<h2>Use the appearance that suits you</h2>
<p>Choose Dark, Light or System. The website remembers your choice in this browser; the app has its own appearance setting.</p>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</Base>
